{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` fails deterministically (exit 128 from `git -C <tmp>/bare.git cat-file -t <oid>`) on any host whose environment injects `safe.bareRepository=explicit` — as this macOS agent harness does via `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0`. At least six prior closed tickets re-diagnosed the same failure as 'known-unrelated'; every session pays that cost again.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed, see comments): under git's `safe.bareRepository=explicit` security policy, `git -C <bare.git>` uses implicit repository discovery, which git refuses for bare repos (`fatal: cannot use bare repository … (safe.bareRepository is 'explicit')`). The push actually succeeds — the object IS in the bare remote — but the test's verification helper `_git()` runs `git -C` against the bare fixture and is refused. Explicit naming via `git --git-dir` is always permitted. The repo already treats this as a portability contract: `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py` asserts bare-repo fixtures survive the explicit policy, and `tests/_git_upkeep.py` / `test_concurrency_regression.py::_bare_git` already use `--git-dir`. `test_ref_lock.py` misses that established pattern — a test-portability defect, not a product bug (production `_ref_lock` never runs `git -C` inside a bare repo).\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the class in the test module: give `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py` a bare-repo-safe git helper that addresses the bare fixture with explicit `--git-dir` naming (matching the `_git_upkeep` prior art) instead of `git -C`, and route the AC0 test's bare-remote inspections (cat-file, rev-parse) through it. Work-tree repos keep `-C`. No production code changes; no retry/skip.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py` (only file).\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN on the existing test itself: it currently fails under the injected `safe.bareRepository=explicit` policy (reproduced deterministically) and must pass after the fix under BOTH postures — the ambient explicit policy and a devnull-global default policy — mirroring the two-posture check in `test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py`. Verify 5x locally plus the full reconciler unit suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause identified with a cited mechanism (recorded on this ticket).\n- [x] `test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` passes in this environment (ambient `safe.bareRepository=explicit`) and under the default policy — verified by running the test 5x locally.\n- [x] Full reconciler suite green afterwards."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787352288589193001,"uuid":"6d4368f2-fe63-4959-b39b-0d6b9048073b"}